      {
        "id": 229852,
        "name": "starkenburg_alexander",
        "username": "starkenburg_alexander",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/starkenburg_alexander/{size}/1857_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-02-25T17:20:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mint after a long slog, with everyone except AZ in the mid 20s at least (including Flora). The only reason AZ was at 3 at the end was I let him redirect a big Thermal Shockwave to end the game rather than healing him back up to full.<br>\n<br>\nBetween Healing Pollen, Flora, and O-X, healing was never an issue. I could have played a lot faster and looser with AZ and KNYFE's HP, but I was worried Bhuta would get one of her monster turns and destroy all my setup. However, after the early game I never saw another destruction card (thanks random shuffles). It was a long slog as I was still targeting every Limb that came out to keep them under control, but eventually AZ got 2x Impales, Cold Snap, Focused Apetures, and Thermal Shockwave out and started dealing consistent damage. The others did some damage as well but not as consistently as AZ.</p>\n<p>Thriya's manipulation of the environment deck meant I could keep Bhuta on whichever side I wanted and avoided the worst of the enviroment cards. She also had 5-6 seeds out at a given time to be destroyed as needed.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>~A-Kat</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:04:42.590Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
